# ======================================================================================================================
# REMARKS & SPECIAL ABILITIES
# ======================================================================================================================
# f2      : Can rename based on EXIF camera model, GPS data, and ID3 audio tags. Built-in 'undo' is elite.
# nomino  : Fastest tool for 1M+ files. JSON mapping allows auditing renames before/after in other tools.
# rnr     : Best 'to-ascii' transliteration. Safest way to fix filenames for cross-platform (Win/Linux) use.
# brename : Designed for CI/CD pipelines. Non-interactive focus with strong overwrite protections.
# qmv     : Part of renameutils. Unique side-by-side editing: Left col = Old Name, Right col = New Name.
# detox   : The "Hammer". Specifically fixes spaces, brackets, and shell-unsafe chars recursively.
# edir    : Detects .git folders and automatically uses 'git mv'. Critical for project history preservation.
# mmv     : Uses positional wildcards (e.g., #1, #2) instead of regex. Very easy for simple batch moves.
# sd      : Not a renamer per se, but the world's fastest regex replacement tool. Used in shell pipelines.

# ======================================================================================================================
# FINAL RECOMMENDATION SUMMARY (EXPANDED)
# ======================================================================================================================
# THE KING       : f2. If you only install one tool, make it this. Best safety, best metadata, best maintenance.
# THE ENGINE     : nomino. If you are a developer handling massive migrations, use this for speed and JSON logging.
# THE CLEANER    : renamex. The modern Rust successor to detox. Use for high-performance normalization of messy files.
# THE TUI        : renux. Best for users who want a visual, interactive interface with live-preview transformations.
# THE SURGEON    : qmv. If you need 100% manual accuracy without learning regex, the side-by-side editor is king.
# THE REPO-FRIEND: edir. If you work in Git, this is the only tool that won't break your 'git blame' history.
# THE VAULT      : rnr. Best for archival work; its dump-file undo system is the most robust for large-scale reverts.
# THE PIPELINE   : sd. Use when you need a high-speed Rust-based regex replacement engine within shell pipelines.
# ======================================================================================================================

